    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Validación cruzada y optimización de hiperparámetros\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "En sección anterior modificamos manualmente diferentes hiperparámetros de Gradient Boosting y XGBoost.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo:\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "    n_estimators=200,\n",
        "    learning_rate=0.05,\n",
        "    max_depth=2\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Sin embargo, inmediatamente aparecieron dos problemas:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. nuestro resultado dependía de una única partición train--validation;\n",
        "2. probar manualmente muchas combinaciones de hiperparámetros resulta poco práctico.\n",
        "\n",
        "Ahora vamos a explorar:\n",
        "\n",
        "- implementar $k$-fold Cross-Validation;\n",
        "- interpretar la media y variabilidad del desempeño entre folds;\n",
        "- utilizar `KFold`;\n",
        "- realizar una búsqueda sistemática con `GridSearchCV`;\n",
        "- realizar una búsqueda aleatoria con `RandomizedSearchCV`;\n",
        "- comparar el costo computacional de ambas estrategias;\n",
        "- integrar preprocesamiento y modelado mediante un `Pipeline`.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.diapositivas}\n",
        "::: {.diapositivas-title}\n",
        "📝 **Diapositivas**\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.diapositivas-body}\n",
        "[Ver diapositivas](https://github.com/CursosENESJuriquilla/TS_Aprendizaje_de_Maquina_2027-1/blob/main/Material/3.2-3.5_ValidacionCruzada_y_GridSearch.pdf)\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preparación\n",
        "\n",
        "Importamos las bibliotecas necesarias."
      ],
      "id": "4c7a79d8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from time import perf_counter\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import fetch_california_housing\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import (\n",
        "    train_test_split,\n",
        "    KFold,\n",
        "    cross_val_score,\n",
        "    GridSearchCV,\n",
        "    RandomizedSearchCV\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingRegressor\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
        "    mean_squared_error,\n",
        "    mean_absolute_error\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "b949a42c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Cargamos nuevamente California Housing."
      ],
      "id": "85f9b5ab"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "housing = fetch_california_housing(as_frame=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "X = housing.data\n",
        "y = housing.target"
      ],
      "id": "e2d713d0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Recordemos las dimensiones:"
      ],
      "id": "d61a50fb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X.shape"
      ],
      "id": "8115293b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Y las características:"
      ],
      "id": "4e2a6b2a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X.columns"
      ],
      "id": "a559f5c8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Reservamos el conjunto de prueba\n",
        "\n",
        "Realizamos exactamente la misma separación utilizada."
      ],
      "id": "10f864fc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    test_size=0.20,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "ef981885",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\"Entrenamiento:\", X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Test:\", X_test.shape)"
      ],
      "id": "92883c16",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "## El test continúa cerrado\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos únicamente:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "X_train\n",
        "y_train\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "para seleccionar hiperparámetros.\n",
        "\n",
        "No utilizaremos `X_test` ni `y_test` para decidir qué configuración funciona mejor.\n",
        "\n",
        "El conjunto de prueba se utilizará para realizar la evaluación final.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## El problema de una única partición\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes dividimos temporalmente el conjunto de entrenamiento en:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{Train}\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "\\begin{cases}\n",
        "\\text{Train GB}\\\\\n",
        "\\text{Validation}\n",
        "\\end{cases}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto nos permitió comparar configuraciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Pero aparece una pregunta:\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Qué ocurre si cambiamos las observaciones que terminaron en el conjunto de validación?\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Vamos a comprobarlo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos primero una configuración fija de Gradient Boosting."
      ],
      "id": "e0dd359b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelo = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "    n_estimators=200,\n",
        "    learning_rate=0.05,\n",
        "    max_depth=2,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "404d1f16",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora realizaremos varias divisiones cambiando únicamente la semilla aleatoria."
      ],
      "id": "bcf54095"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados_split = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for semilla in [1, 10, 42, 100, 500]:\n",
        "\n",
        "    X_tr, X_val, y_tr, y_val = train_test_split(\n",
        "        X_train,\n",
        "        y_train,\n",
        "        test_size=0.20,\n",
        "        random_state=semilla\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    modelo.fit(X_tr, y_tr)\n",
        "\n",
        "    pred = modelo.predict(X_val)\n",
        "\n",
        "    rmse = np.sqrt(\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(y_val, pred)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    resultados_split.append({\n",
        "        \"random_state\": semilla,\n",
        "        \"RMSE\": rmse\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "df_split = pd.DataFrame(resultados_split)\n",
        "\n",
        "df_split"
      ],
      "id": "f60b1e38",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Visualicemos los resultados."
      ],
      "id": "4da0059f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    df_split[\"random_state\"].astype(str),\n",
        "    df_split[\"RMSE\"],\n",
        "    marker=\"o\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Partición\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"RMSE de validación\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"El resultado depende de la partición\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "a5512654",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "El modelo es esencialmente el mismo en todos los casos. Entonces, ¿por qué obtenemos distintos valores de RMSE?\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "La evaluación depende de qué observaciones fueron utilizadas para entrenar y cuáles fueron utilizadas para validar.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por eso es importante **Cross-Validation**.\n",
        "\n",
        "## $k$-fold Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "En $k$-fold Cross-Validation dividimos los datos en $k$ subconjuntos o *folds*:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "D_1,D_2,\\ldots,D_k.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Cada fold se utiliza una vez como conjunto de validación y los restantes se utilizan para entrenamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, para $k=5$ realizamos cinco entrenamientos.\n",
        "\n",
        "El desempeño promedio es\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\overline{s}_{CV}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{k}\n",
        "\\sum_{j=1}^{k}s_j.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "También podemos estudiar su variabilidad mediante la desviación estándar.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Nuestro primer Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "Crearemos una estrategia de 5-fold Cross-Validation."
      ],
      "id": "a54e7e0f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "cv = KFold(\n",
        "    n_splits=5,\n",
        "    shuffle=True,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "564310a5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Utilizaremos el mismo Gradient Boosting:"
      ],
      "id": "312fc708"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelo = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "    n_estimators=200,\n",
        "    learning_rate=0.05,\n",
        "    max_depth=2,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "91cdc32d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora utilizamos `cross_val_score()`."
      ],
      "id": "2ec81dc2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "scores = cross_val_score(\n",
        "    modelo,\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train,\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "ee8cf23a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Veamos el resultado:"
      ],
      "id": "475dc74d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "scores"
      ],
      "id": "289c9260",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Puede llamar la atención que los valores sean negativos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto ocurre porque `scikit-learn` utiliza la convención de que un *score* mayor debe representar un mejor desempeño.\n",
        "\n",
        "Sin embargo, RMSE es un error:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{menor RMSE}\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{mejor}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello, `scikit-learn` devuelve:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "-\\operatorname{RMSE}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Para trabajar directamente con RMSE podemos cambiar el signo:"
      ],
      "id": "c9967391"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "rmse_cv = -scores\n",
        "\n",
        "rmse_cv"
      ],
      "id": "42f67679",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Desempeño promedio\n",
        "\n",
        "Calculamos ahora la media:"
      ],
      "id": "b91855fd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "rmse_cv.mean()"
      ],
      "id": "7bbee34e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y la desviación estándar:"
      ],
      "id": "fde49a61"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "rmse_cv.std()"
      ],
      "id": "0ec144b9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos reportar:"
      ],
      "id": "1463d8c6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\n",
        "    f\"RMSE CV: {rmse_cv.mean():.4f} \"\n",
        "    f\"+/- {rmse_cv.std():.4f}\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "8774a251",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Por ejemplo, conceptualmente obtenemos algo de la forma\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{RMSE}_{CV}\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\overline{\\operatorname{RMSE}}\n",
        "\\pm\n",
        "SD.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Cross-Validation nos proporciona más de un número\n",
        "\n",
        "La media nos informa sobre el desempeño promedio.\n",
        "\n",
        "La desviación estándar nos ayuda a observar cuánto cambia el resultado entre diferentes particiones.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Visualización de los folds\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos visualizar los cinco resultados obtenidos."
      ],
      "id": "d6b428af"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    range(1, len(rmse_cv) + 1),\n",
        "    rmse_cv,\n",
        "    marker=\"o\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.axhline(\n",
        "    rmse_cv.mean(),\n",
        "    linestyle=\"--\",\n",
        "    label=\"RMSE promedio\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Fold\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"RMSE\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"RMSE en cada fold\")\n",
        "plt.xticks(range(1, 6))\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "c6d1b1ea",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Todos los folds producen exactamente el mismo resultado?\n",
        "¿Por qué es más informativo observar los cinco resultados que una única partición train--validation?\n",
        "\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparando algunas configuraciones\n",
        "\n",
        "Antes comparamos manualmente diferentes configuraciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Hagámoslo nuevamente, pero ahora utilizando Cross-Validation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Consideremos:"
      ],
      "id": "2ee6bed9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "configuraciones = [\n",
        "    (\"A\", 0.1, 100, 2),\n",
        "    (\"B\", 0.05, 200, 2),\n",
        "    (\"C\", 0.01, 500, 2),\n",
        "    (\"D\", 0.1, 100, 4)\n",
        "]"
      ],
      "id": "a7bbc3fa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Evaluaremos cada configuración con exactamente los mismos folds."
      ],
      "id": "50fb0f9e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados_cv = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for nombre, lr, n_est, depth in configuraciones:\n",
        "\n",
        "    modelo = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "        learning_rate=lr,\n",
        "        n_estimators=n_est,\n",
        "        max_depth=depth,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    scores = cross_val_score(\n",
        "        modelo,\n",
        "        X_train,\n",
        "        y_train,\n",
        "        cv=cv,\n",
        "        scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    rmse = -scores\n",
        "\n",
        "    resultados_cv.append({\n",
        "        \"Modelo\": nombre,\n",
        "        \"learning_rate\": lr,\n",
        "        \"n_estimators\": n_est,\n",
        "        \"max_depth\": depth,\n",
        "        \"RMSE_CV\": rmse.mean(),\n",
        "        \"SD_CV\": rmse.std()\n",
        "    })"
      ],
      "id": "e9ab95c6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos una tabla."
      ],
      "id": "09347391"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_cv = pd.DataFrame(resultados_cv)\n",
        "\n",
        "df_cv"
      ],
      "id": "67263cc0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora nuestra comparación ya no depende de una única partición.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Visualización\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos representar el RMSE promedio junto con su variabilidad."
      ],
      "id": "bfc8dab8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.errorbar(\n",
        "    df_cv[\"Modelo\"],\n",
        "    df_cv[\"RMSE_CV\"],\n",
        "    yerr=df_cv[\"SD_CV\"],\n",
        "    fmt=\"o\",\n",
        "    capsize=5\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Configuración\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"RMSE de Cross-Validation\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Comparación mediante 5-fold Cross-Validation\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "c37efd76",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "Las barras muestran la variabilidad entre folds.\n",
        "\n",
        "Una diferencia pequeña entre dos medias no debe interpretarse automáticamente como una diferencia importante entre los modelos.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## El problema de la búsqueda manual\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora evaluamos únicamente cuatro configuraciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Pero podríamos querer explorar:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\texttt{learning\\_rate}\n",
        "\\in\n",
        "\\{0.01,0.05,0.1\\},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\texttt{n\\_estimators}\n",
        "\\in\n",
        "\\{100,200,500\\},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "y\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_depth}\n",
        "\\in\n",
        "\\{2,3,4\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "¿Cuántas configuraciones tenemos?"
      ],
      "id": "0710fd45"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "3 * 3 * 3"
      ],
      "id": "2459f32a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Son:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "3\\times3\\times3=27\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "configuraciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Pero cada configuración se evalúa mediante 5-fold Cross-Validation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por lo tanto:"
      ],
      "id": "a27c6301"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "27 * 5"
      ],
      "id": "3039e4c9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "necesitamos al menos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "27\\times5=135\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "ajustes del modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Escribir manualmente los ciclos necesarios sería posible, pero `scikit-learn` proporciona herramientas específicamente diseñadas para este proceso.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Grid Search\n",
        "\n",
        "`GridSearchCV` evalúa sistemáticamente todas las combinaciones que especifiquemos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Definimos primero nuestra cuadrícula."
      ],
      "id": "36d1eaba"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"learning_rate\": [0.01, 0.05, 0.1],\n",
        "    \"n_estimators\": [100, 200, 500],\n",
        "    \"max_depth\": [2, 3, 4]\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "12479c39",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos calcular el número de configuraciones:"
      ],
      "id": "820b6e58"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "n_configuraciones = (\n",
        "    len(param_grid[\"learning_rate\"])\n",
        "    * len(param_grid[\"n_estimators\"])\n",
        "    * len(param_grid[\"max_depth\"])\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(n_configuraciones)"
      ],
      "id": "9eeb418a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos la búsqueda."
      ],
      "id": "5b144377"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelo = GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "grid_search = GridSearchCV(\n",
        "    estimator=modelo,\n",
        "    param_grid=param_grid,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    n_jobs=1,\n",
        "    return_train_score=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "#grid_search.fit(X_train, y_train)"
      ],
      "id": "8bf2c1d4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "## `n_jobs=-1`\n",
        "\n",
        "Con `n_jobs=-1`, `scikit-learn` puede utilizar los procesadores disponibles para ejecutar parte del trabajo en paralelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto puede reducir considerablemente el tiempo de búsqueda. En una computadora de 32GB de ram y 12 CPUs, lo recomendable es `n_jobs=4`.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Ejecutamos la búsqueda\n",
        "\n",
        "Vamos a medir también cuánto tarda."
      ],
      "id": "54ddd732"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "inicio = perf_counter()\n",
        "\n",
        "grid_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "tiempo_grid = perf_counter() - inicio\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Tiempo: {tiempo_grid:.2f} segundos\")"
      ],
      "id": "22b6b409",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Resultados de Grid Search\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos consultar directamente la configuración seleccionada."
      ],
      "id": "8031655f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "grid_search.best_params_"
      ],
