      "id": "a2026927",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Esto nos permite observar que Grid Search no produce solamente una configuración.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos estudiar el comportamiento de todo el espacio que decidimos explorar.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Visualizando una parte de la búsqueda\n",
        "\n",
        "Para visualizar los resultados fijaremos, por ejemplo,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\texttt{max\\_depth}=2.\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "786e6b58"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "grid_depth2 = resultados_grid[\n",
        "    resultados_grid[\"param_max_depth\"] == 2\n",
        "].copy()"
      ],
      "id": "2c340509",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora podemos representar el RMSE para diferentes combinaciones de `learning_rate` y `n_estimators`."
      ],
      "id": "a5ca34ac"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "for lr in sorted(\n",
        "    grid_depth2[\"param_learning_rate\"].unique()\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    datos = grid_depth2[\n",
        "        grid_depth2[\"param_learning_rate\"] == lr\n",
        "    ].sort_values(\"param_n_estimators\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.plot(\n",
        "        datos[\"param_n_estimators\"],\n",
        "        datos[\"RMSE_CV\"],\n",
        "        marker=\"o\",\n",
        "        label=f\"learning_rate = {lr}\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"n_estimators\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"RMSE CV\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Interacción entre learning rate y número de árboles\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "37aeef59",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Esta gráfica nos permite recuperar una idea de la práctica anterior:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\texttt{learning\\_rate}\n",
        "\\quad\\text{y}\\quad\n",
        "\\texttt{n\\_estimators}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "no deben interpretarse necesariamente de manera aislada.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Qué limitación tiene Grid Search?\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestra búsqueda anterior utilizó solamente tres hiperparámetros.\n",
        "\n",
        "Supongamos ahora que queremos explorar:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "learning_rate\n",
        "n_estimators\n",
        "max_depth\n",
        "subsample\n",
        "min_samples_leaf\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "y que consideramos cinco valores para cada uno.\n",
        "\n",
        "El número de configuraciones sería\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "5^5=3125.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Con 5-fold Cross-Validation:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "3125\\times5=15625\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "ajustes del modelo."
      ],
      "id": "f415185d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "5**5 * 5"
      ],
      "id": "6c26ad00",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "El costo crece rápidamente.\n",
        "\n",
        "Además, para variables continuas como `learning_rate`, una cuadrícula solamente evalúa los valores específicos que nosotros elegimos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto motiva una estrategia diferente.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Random Search\n",
        "\n",
        "En Random Search especificamos un espacio de búsqueda, pero evaluamos solamente un número determinado de configuraciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, podemos decidir:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "B=20.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto significa que evaluaremos únicamente 20 configuraciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Con 5-fold Cross-Validation:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "20\\times5=100\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "ajustes principales del modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Definimos el espacio de búsqueda\n",
        "\n",
        "Para aprovechar mejor Random Search podemos utilizar distribuciones continuas.\n",
        "\n",
        "Importamos:"
      ],
      "id": "a07331f9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from scipy.stats import randint, loguniform, uniform"
      ],
      "id": "991f682b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Definimos:"
      ],
      "id": "a1f8ffa7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_distributions = {\n",
        "    \"n_estimators\": randint(100, 601),\n",
        "    \"learning_rate\": loguniform(0.01, 0.2),\n",
        "    \"max_depth\": randint(1, 6),\n",
        "    \"subsample\": uniform(0.6, 0.4)\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "e4ed6f4b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Aquí:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `randint(100, 601)` genera enteros entre 100 y 600;\n",
        "- `loguniform(0.01, 0.2)` explora valores positivos de `learning_rate` en escala logarítmica;\n",
        "- `randint(1, 6)` genera profundidades entre 1 y 5;\n",
        "- `uniform(0.6, 0.4)` genera valores entre 0.6 y 1.0.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## ¿Por qué `loguniform` para learning rate?\n",
        "\n",
        "Para hiperparámetros positivos que pueden variar en diferentes órdenes de magnitud, puede ser más informativo explorar una escala logarítmica.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, queremos distinguir adecuadamente entre valores cercanos a\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "0.01,\\quad 0.1\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "en lugar de concentrar el muestreo únicamente en diferencias absolutas.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## RandomizedSearchCV\n",
        "\n",
        "Construimos la búsqueda."
      ],
      "id": "a5e4883b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "random_search = RandomizedSearchCV(\n",
        "    estimator=GradientBoostingRegressor(\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    param_distributions=param_distributions,\n",
        "    n_iter=20,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    n_jobs=1,\n",
        "    return_train_score=True\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "07f29954",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ejecutamos y medimos el tiempo."
      ],
      "id": "df419c88"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "inicio = perf_counter()\n",
        "\n",
        "random_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "tiempo_random = perf_counter() - inicio\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Tiempo: {tiempo_random:.2f} segundos\")"
      ],
      "id": "955067fb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Resultados de Random Search\n",
        "\n",
        "Consultamos la configuración seleccionada."
      ],
      "id": "33266e2c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "random_search.best_params_"
      ],
      "id": "b9ee195b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Y su RMSE promedio:"
      ],
      "id": "329241ea"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "best_rmse_random = -random_search.best_score_\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Mejor RMSE CV: {best_rmse_random:.4f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "f8c43f8d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos recuperar nuevamente todos los resultados."
      ],
      "id": "e9bfb2c7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados_random = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    random_search.cv_results_\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "resultados_random[\"RMSE_CV\"] = (\n",
        "    -resultados_random[\"mean_test_score\"]\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "270093fc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Veamos las mejores configuraciones:"
      ],
      "id": "307c7022"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "resultados_random[\n",
        "    [\n",
        "        \"param_learning_rate\",\n",
        "        \"param_n_estimators\",\n",
        "        \"param_max_depth\",\n",
        "        \"param_subsample\",\n",
        "        \"RMSE_CV\",\n",
        "        \"mean_fit_time\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "].sort_values(\"RMSE_CV\").head(10)"
      ],
      "id": "2f92641a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Grid Search vs. Random Search\n",
        "\n",
        "Construyamos una comparación sencilla."
      ],
      "id": "2af33393"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comparacion_busquedas = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Método\": [\n",
        "        \"Grid Search\",\n",
        "        \"Random Search\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Configuraciones evaluadas\": [\n",
        "        len(resultados_grid),\n",
        "        len(resultados_random)\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"RMSE CV\": [\n",
        "        best_rmse_grid,\n",
        "        best_rmse_random\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Tiempo (s)\": [\n",
        "        tiempo_grid,\n",
        "        tiempo_random\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "comparacion_busquedas"
      ],
      "id": "5b4af6e3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Es importante interpretar esta tabla con cuidado.\n",
        "\n",
        "Las dos búsquedas no exploraron exactamente el mismo espacio:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Grid Search utilizó una cuadrícula discreta;\n",
        "- Random Search utilizó distribuciones más amplias;\n",
        "- Random Search exploró `subsample`, mientras que nuestra cuadrícula inicial no lo hizo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por lo tanto, esta comparación tiene principalmente un objetivo didáctico.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "## No buscamos demostrar que un método \"gana\"\n",
        "\n",
        "El objetivo es observar dos estrategias diferentes.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Grid Search**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "evalúa todas las combinaciones de una cuadrícula especificada.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Random Search**\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\longrightarrow\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "permite fijar directamente un presupuesto de configuraciones mediante `n_iter`.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Y XGBoost?\n",
        "\n",
        "Exactamente las mismas herramientas pueden utilizarse con XGBoost.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo:"
      ],
      "id": "bbe66db6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from xgboost import XGBRegressor"
      ],
      "id": "0dd861b8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podríamos definir:"
      ],
      "id": "f5a4ab62"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "xgb = XGBRegressor(\n",
        "    objective=\"reg:squarederror\",\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    n_jobs=1\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "378212a7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y un espacio como:"
      ],
      "id": "587871f1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_xgb = {\n",
        "    \"n_estimators\": [100, 300, 500],\n",
        "    \"learning_rate\": [0.01, 0.05, 0.1],\n",
        "    \"max_depth\": [2, 3, 5],\n",
        "    \"subsample\": [0.7, 0.9, 1.0],\n",
        "    \"colsample_bytree\": [0.7, 0.9, 1.0]\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "1a64865a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Pero observa cuántas combinaciones produce:"
      ],
      "id": "0cc16ac4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "3**5"
      ],
      "id": "0f808df3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Tenemos\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "3^5=243\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "configuraciones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Con 5-fold Cross-Validation:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "243\\times5=1215\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "ajustes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por esta razón, para espacios como éste suele ser más atractivo comenzar con una búsqueda aleatoria.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "No ejecutaremos esta búsqueda completa durante la clase.\n",
        "\n",
        "El objetivo es reconocer que las mismas herramientas pueden aplicarse a diferentes estimadores compatibles con la interfaz de `scikit-learn`.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preprocesamiento y Cross-Validation\n",
        "\n",
        "California Housing tiene una ventaja para nuestro ejemplo de Gradient Boosting: los modelos basados en árboles no requieren estandarización para construir sus divisiones.\n",
        "\n",
        "Pero imaginemos que utilizamos un modelo que sí depende de la escala de las variables.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podríamos pensar en hacer(no correr):\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "scaler.fit(X_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train_scaled = scaler.transform(X_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "cross_val_score(\n",
        "    modelo,\n",
        "    X_train_scaled,\n",
        "    y_train,\n",
        "    cv=cv\n",
        ")\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Sin embargo, existe un problema.\n",
        "\n",
        "El escalador aprendió sus parámetros utilizando **todo `X_train`** antes de construir los folds.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, `StandardScaler` utiliza\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "z\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Si calculamos $\\mu$ y $\\sigma$ utilizando todo `X_train`, las observaciones que posteriormente pertenecerán al validation fold ya participaron en el preprocesamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto constituye una forma de **data leakage**.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Pipelines\n",
        "\n",
        "La solución es incluir las transformaciones que aprenden de los datos dentro de un `Pipeline`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para ilustrarlo utilizaremos un modelo que ellos ya conocen: regresión lineal regularizada."
      ],
      "id": "ab871ed7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge"
      ],
      "id": "45e30531",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos:"
      ],
      "id": "c602900a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
        "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
        "    (\"model\", Ridge())\n",
        "])"
      ],
      "id": "f2b22ddb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora realizamos Cross-Validation sobre **todo el pipeline**."
      ],
      "id": "fe81158a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "scores_ridge = cross_val_score(\n",
        "    pipeline,\n",
        "    X_train,\n",
        "    y_train,\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "rmse_ridge = -scores_ridge\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    f\"RMSE CV: {rmse_ridge.mean():.4f} \"\n",
        "    f\"+/- {rmse_ridge.std():.4f}\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "fef94a39",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Durante cada fold, `scikit-learn` realiza conceptualmente:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{training fold}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\downarrow\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{ajustar StandardScaler}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\downarrow\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{transformar training fold}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\downarrow\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{entrenar Ridge}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "y solamente después utiliza esos parámetros para transformar el validation fold.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tuning dentro de un Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "También podemos optimizar hiperparámetros dentro de un pipeline.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para referirnos a un hiperparámetro utilizamos:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "nombre_del_paso__nombre_del_hiperparametro\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo:"
      ],
      "id": "6253fc9a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "param_grid_ridge = {\n",
        "    \"model__alpha\": [0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100]\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "a8a4d967",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Construimos la búsqueda:"
      ],
      "id": "cd76ca5d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "grid_ridge = GridSearchCV(\n",
        "    estimator=pipeline,\n",
        "    param_grid=param_grid_ridge,\n",
        "    cv=cv,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        "    n_jobs=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "grid_ridge.fit(X_train, y_train)"
      ],
      "id": "aad2061d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Consultamos:"
      ],
      "id": "d3fac0ce"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "grid_ridge.best_params_"
      ],
      "id": "0c52a4b3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y:"
      ],
      "id": "139b3661"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "-grid_ridge.best_score_"
      ],
      "id": "36c4eb41",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "## La idea central\n",
        "\n",
        "Cuando una operación aprende información de los datos, debe formar parte del procedimiento que se valida.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\boxed{\n",
        "\\text{imputación}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{escalamiento}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{selección de variables}\n",
        "\\rightarrow\n",
        "\\text{modelo}\n",
        "}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "puede constituir un único pipeline.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Qué ocurre después de la búsqueda?\n",
        "\n",
        "Cuando ejecutamos:\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "grid_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "`GridSearchCV`:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. evalúa las configuraciones mediante Cross-Validation;\n",
        "2. identifica la configuración seleccionada;\n",
        "3. por defecto vuelve a entrenar esa configuración utilizando **todo `X_train`**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Este último paso se conoce como **refit**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos comprobar que:"
      ],
      "id": "0d3dc317"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "grid_search.refit"
      ],
      "id": "a7ba3fd2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y recuperar el modelo reajustado:"
      ],
      "id": "0308c252"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "modelo_seleccionado = grid_search.best_estimator_\n",
        "\n",
        "modelo_seleccionado"
      ],
      "id": "001ef9b3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
